Ladybird centers the shadow contents of a native block input in
the final height of its content box when a min/max constraint
sets that height. WebKit’s RenderTextControlSingleLine::layout
positions the inner editor and placeholder against the input’s
final size. Gecko’s nsTextControlFrame::Reflow lays out the control
as a scroll frame. Blink builds the editing viewport and inner
editor in EditingViewPortElement::CustomStyleForLayoutObject and
TextControlInnerEditorElement::CustomStyleForLayoutObject.

In the 44px ChargeMap reduction, Firefox 151.0 and WebKit 26.5
painted identical text pixels for height and min-height. Chrome
158.0.8127.37 differed by one pixel vertically. All three centered
the text in both controls.
